# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  The Boogeyman: keys and settings
#
#  1. Copy this file:        make env      (or: cp .env.example .env)
#  2. Paste your keys into .env (NOT this file).
#  3. Restart the app (make dev).
#
#  .env is gitignored (so is brain/.env, which also still works). Keys stay on your machine and never reach the UI.
#  Never commit a real key, and never paste one into an issue or chat.
#
#  Minimum to get him talking: ELEVENLABS_API_KEY + GROQ_API_KEY (both free).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── 1. VOICE: ElevenLabs (hearing you + speaking). Required for voice. ───────
#
#  Get it (free plan is enough):
#    1. Sign up at https://elevenlabs.io
#    2. Profile (bottom left) → API Keys → Create API key
#    3. Under permissions, give it at least:
#         Text to Speech: Access
#         Speech to Text: Access
#         Voices:         Read
#    4. Copy the key (starts with sk_) and paste it below.
#
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# The voice he speaks with. Default is "Brian" (deep, premade, works on the free plan).
# To use another one: open a voice in your ElevenLabs Voices page → copy its Voice ID.
ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=nPczCjzI2devNBz1zQrb

# Models (defaults are fast and cheap; leave as is unless you know why).
# ELEVENLABS_TTS_MODEL=eleven_flash_v2_5
# ELEVENLABS_STT_MODEL=scribe_v2


# ── 2. BRAIN: the AI that thinks and replies. Set at least ONE. ──────────────
#
#  Without any of these he still hears and speaks, but only knows a few
#  built-in lines and the instant commands (shut down, work mode, etc.).
#
#  Groq (free, fast, recommended to start):
#    1. Sign up at https://console.groq.com
#    2. API Keys → Create API Key
#    3. Copy the key (starts with gsk_) and paste it below.
#  The free tier has per-minute and per-day limits; when one model runs out he
#  automatically moves to the next free model.
#
GROQ_API_KEY=

#  Anthropic Claude (paid, smartest). Get a key at https://console.anthropic.com
#  If this is set, he uses Claude first (with LLM_PROVIDER=auto).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

#  Which brain to use: auto (Anthropic if set, else Groq) | groq | anthropic | openai
# LLM_PROVIDER=auto

#  Override the model. Defaults: openai/gpt-oss-120b on Groq, claude-haiku-5-5 on Anthropic.
# LLM_MODEL=

#  Any other OpenAI-compatible API (OpenRouter, Gemini, a local server...):
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=
# LLM_MODEL=


# ── 3. OPTIONAL TUNING ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Microphone by name or index. List them with:  brain/.venv/bin/python -m sounddevice
# BOOGEYMAN_MIC=

# 0 turns voice off entirely (UI only).
# BOOGEYMAN_VOICE=1

# Talking over him makes him stop and listen. If he cuts himself off on loud
# speakers, raise the level (e.g. 1.5) or turn it off with 0. Headphones fix it.
# BOOGEYMAN_BARGE_IN=1
# BOOGEYMAN_BARGE_LEVEL=1.0

# How many recent messages go with each reply (fewer = lasts longer on free limits).
# BOOGEYMAN_HISTORY=12

# Where memory.json lives (default: ~/.local/share/boogeyman).
# BOOGEYMAN_DATA=

# Research (web search) uses DuckDuckGo through the ddgs package: free, no key needed.
